WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
We have three polynomials,
c of P, d of P, and g of P,

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:10.813
built from the same four sign
polynomials, H zero through H three.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.500
Let us use that common origin
to build a polynomial E of P

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.080
whose coefficients all
become one modulo one plus i.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:25.560
For u equal to three, our target is
one plus P, through P to the eighth.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.720
Call that all ones polynomial J of P.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.460
We want E of P to connect
two parts of the proof.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.060
Expressing it through c, d, and g
lets us use their comparisons later.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.640
Expressing it through the H polynomials
will reveal its coefficient residues.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.840
The combination we choose is d of
P minus c of P, divided by two,

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.300
plus g of P minus c of
P, divided by one plus i.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:58.160
Let us see why adding these terms
gives the all ones congruence.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.580
Substitute the definitions from
Node three. The H zero terms cancel.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.700
The first quotient becomes minus the
sum of H one of P and H three of P,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.240
divided by two. The second
quotient becomes minus

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.870
the sum of H two of P and H
three of P, divided by two.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.700
Add i times the sum of H
one of P and H two of P,

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:30.060
divided by two. Every half sum
here has integer coefficients:

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.880
adding two signs always
gives an even integer.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.500
We form these exact quotients
in the original ring,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.440
before reducing coefficients.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.260
Now add the expressions.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:47.080
The two halves of negative H
three of P combine into a whole.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.980
Collecting the other terms
gives E of P equal to

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:56.920
negative H three of P, plus
the factor i minus one,

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.900
multiplied by the half sum
of H one of P and H two of P.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.140
This identity is the useful
feature of our definition.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.260
Reduce modulo one plus i.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:14.180
Since i minus one equals i
times the sum one plus i,

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.540
the entire second term disappears.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:21.040
We are left with the residue
of negative H three of P.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.430
Every remaining coefficient
is positive or negative one.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.980
These signs have the same residue
because their difference, two,

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:33.060
is the product of one
plus i and one minus i.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.160
Both signs therefore become
one modulo one plus i.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.030
Keep every power of P in place and
replace its coefficient by one.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.020
In our nine position example,
E of P is congruent to J of P:

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:52.000
one plus P plus P squared,
through P to the eighth.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:57.260
This is a congruence, not an
equality of the original polynomials.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.150
Finally substitute P equal to one.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.100
Each of the nine terms becomes
one. Pair eight of those ones.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.340
Every pair is two, which
vanishes modulo one plus i.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.280
One unpaired one remains.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.740
Thus E of one is congruent
to J of one, which is nine,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:22.600
and nine is congruent to one. The same
calculation works for general odd u.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:27.300
There are u squared terms in
J of P, and u squared is odd.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.280
J of one equals u squared.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.060
Therefore E of one is congruent
to one modulo one plus i.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.840
The common signs gave
the all ones polynomial;

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.140
the odd number of terms
gives this final residue.
